{"The logger 'log' with additional context values (name, kind, method) was created but the original struct logger d.Log is being added to the context instead, so downstream functions won't have the specific request context in their logs.": 0.9927327036857605, "In case of an error during d.Storage.Create operation, recordLegacyDuration is called instead of recordStorageDuration, incorrectly attributing the error and duration to legacy instead of storage.": 0.9992885589599609, "The recordStorageDuration function's third parameter is for the kind of the object, but name (the object's name) is passed, creating high-cardinality metrics which can cause significant performance issues for Prometheus. Should use options.Kind instead.": 0.9564132690429688, "The goroutine inherits the context from the parent request, so if the client cancels the request after the primary storage operation succeeds, the goroutine will also be cancelled, preventing the legacy write. Should use context.Background() to ensure the legacy write is attempted regardless of the client's connection state.": 0.910316526889801, "If the legacy operation fails, the error is only recorded as a metric but not logged, making debugging difficult. These errors should be logged.": 0.9469534754753113, "The metric recording for legacy DeleteCollection operation calls recordStorageDuration instead of recordLegacyDuration, incorrectly attributing the duration to storage instead of legacy.": 0.9996569156646729, "Test case for error when creating an object in unified store uses setupLegacyFn instead of setupStorageFn to set up the mock, which is misleading and makes the test harder to understand.": 0.7868697047233582}